- How would you seed and rotate the allowlist safely?
- How to handle missing tenant or Redis latency?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design tenant-aware rate limiting and observability in CNF gateways, a realistic production concern for multi-tenant platforms used by large companies.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant-scoped policy API (REST)
- Sidecar token bucket limiter with TTL cache
- Real-time policy fetch and rotation
- Central audit/log sink and schema

## Code Example

```javascript
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(capacity, fillRate) {
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.fillRate = fillRate;
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.lastRefill = Date.now();
  }
  allow(n = 1) {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.lastRefill) / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + elapsed * this.fillRate);
    this.lastRefill = now;
    if (this.tokens >= n) {
      this.tokens -= n;
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle policy drift during high load?
- What approaches ensure audit integrity and privacy?

